 3. How to use the output files

 Plugin .zip files (dist/{name}.zip)

 Upload to Claude Desktop:
 1. Build: python tools/build-plugin.py --plugin product-discovery --confirm
 2. Go to Claude Desktop > Settings > Plugins > Upload
 3. Select dist/product-discovery.zip
 4. Skills become available in conversations

 Plugin build directories (dist/build/{name}/)

 For marketplace install (anyone with the GitHub repo):
 1. They run: /plugin install product-discovery@AmitSinghJ2Engg/skill-share
 2. Claude reads .claude-plugin/marketplace.json which points to ./dist/build/product-discovery
 3. Skills are installed directly from the git repo

 For local testing:
 claude --plugin-dir dist/build/product-discovery

 Skill manifest (dist/skill-manifest.json)

 For Claude sessions that need system awareness:
 - A skill or task can read this file to understand what skills exist, their modes, sizes, and dependencies
 - Useful for the ism-skill-factory or ism-gap-auditor skills (future) that need to reason about the system

 For you (Amit) to check system health:
 - Open it to see budget percentages (e.g., product-discovery at 94% of 70KB limit)
 - See which skills are missing SKILL.md
 - See which skills aren't assigned to any plugin yet

 Key sections:
 - plugins.{name}.budget_pct -- how close each plugin is to the 70KB limit
 - coverage.skills_placeholder_only -- skills that need SKILL.md written
 - coverage.skills_on_disk_not_in_registry -- skills not assigned to any plugin
 - validation.checks_failed -- quick health check number

 Marketplace JSON (.claude-plugin/marketplace.json)

 Purpose: Lets other users install your plugins from GitHub. Currently lists only product-discovery (the only built plugin). Run --update-marketplace after building more plugins to auto-add them.

